The Venn diagram shows a survey of $45$ students, where $J$ is 'the student has a part-time job' and $B$ is 'the student catches the bus to school'. What effect does the condition 'given that the student catches the bus' have on the sample space?

questions.solution_text:
1. **Reduce the sample space to the condition**
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{patterns}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\begin{scope}
\clip (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\fill[gray!35] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\end{scope}
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw[thick] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$J$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$B$};
\node at (2.15,2.3) {$10$};
\node at (4,2.3) {$12$};
\node at (5.85,2.3) {$18$};
\node at (7.3,0.5) {$8$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Let $x$ be the number in both events. The four regions must add to $48$.
$(30 - x) + x + (22 - x) + 8 = 48$
$60 - x = 48$
$x = 12$
The condition reduces the sample space to the $30$ students inside the thick circle.
2. **Count the favourable outcomes inside it**
Of those $30$, the $12$ in the shaded region have a part-time job.
3. **Write the fraction and simplify**
$P(J \mid B) = \frac{12}{30}$
$= \frac{2}{5}$
